  "notes": [
    "This amendment chains directly to the byte-exact immutable original consumed-test ledger. No prior Stage-90 amendment, result, prediction surface, scratch directory, or checkpoint is a parent or input.",
    "Within each target and held fold, labels opened only under that fold plan's support capability score the eight frozen A1 source actions against B by exact pooled BACC. S4 selects the highest strictly positive gain with a deterministic numeric-source tie break; a support aggregate lacking either class or absence of a positive authorized gain returns exactly B.",
    "B, U, and all eight A1 probabilities seal globally before any labels open. For every (H,f), its S4 decision and seal precede opening labels under the evaluation capability for that same (H,f); labels used as support in one rotation never gain evaluation authority in another. G_static scores each candidate e by equal-center mean exact gain over donor query centers q not in {H,e} and returns B unless the best gain is strictly positive. No case feature, donor model, target-local calibration, threshold selection, or hyperparameter search is admitted. O_static and O_case are terminal bounds only.",
    "The fixed null permutes complete A1 sufficient-statistic contribution blocks, never labels: each support case gets a SHA-256 candidate order, each null index applies a counter-SplitMix64 nonzero cyclic shift in 1 through 7, B stays fixed, and the same S4 selection rule is recomputed. The null plan for each (H,f) seals before that plan's evaluation capability opens.",
    "The only uncertainty summaries are descriptive two-sided t8 intervals over nine center contrasts and descriptive permutation-null exceedance counts and fractions. No confirmatory p-value, success gate, route, action, policy, promotion, deployment, or later-experiment authority can result."
  ]
